# Rank 1670 / CVE-2018-12584: resiprocate's connection-based SIP transports
# accumulate a partially received body in a heap buffer and treat the
# Content-Length header as the body's exact size. ConnectionBase::preparseNewBytes
# (resip/stack/ConnectionBase.cxx), in its PartialBody state, adds the bytes just
# read to the fill position and then decides the body is complete with an exact
# equality:
#
#   contentLength = mMessage->const_header(h_ContentLength).value();
#   mBufferPos += bytesRead;
#   if (mBufferPos == contentLength) { ...body complete... }
#   else if (mBufferPos == mBufferSize)
#   {
#      size_t newSize = resipMin(mBufferSize*3/2, contentLength);
#      char* newBuffer = new char[newSize];
#      memcpy(newBuffer, mBuffer, mBufferSize);      // ConnectionBase.cxx:534 at the parent
#      mBufferSize = newSize;
#   }
#
# Content-Length is validated only against an upper bound (messageSizeMax), and
# the growth branch sizes the new buffer from that same attacker-declared value.
# A read that carries the rest of the body plus the start of the next message
# makes mBufferPos overshoot contentLength, so the equality fails, the buffer-full
# branch runs, and the copy writes mBufferSize bytes into a buffer allocated with
# min(mBufferSize*3/2, contentLength) < mBufferSize — a heap overwrite (the
# upstream message: "the stack could crash if a TCP based sender sends a
# Content-Length smaller than the actual SIP body transmitted"). The fixing commit
# 2cb291191c93c7c4e371e22cb89805a5b31d6608 changes the guard to
# `mBufferPos >= contentLength`, carries the over-long tail into a fresh buffer,
# and documents the growth branch's precondition with
# `assert(contentLength >= mBufferSize)`. The growth-branch memcpy itself is
# untouched at both revisions: what changes is whether that branch is reachable with a
# completed body. Verified at the parent (the equality guard and the
# min-with-contentLength allocation are present) and at the fixed revision (the >= guard,
# the overhang copy and the assert are present).
#
# Re-measured at the current tip, both directions.
#
# 1. The extraction blocker the first pass pinned is gone. ccConv.stmt now lowers
# a labelled statement (c.go:1137), so preparseNewBytes' whole `start:` switch is
# in the graph: `vyql match` on the real file labels the growth arithmetic
# (code.ComputedSizeValue, code.IntegerSizeArithmetic at :523) and the copy
# (code.RawMemoryCopySize at :534), where the first pass measured zero labels
# between :135 and :590. The last two snippets below are that extraction fix's
# minimal pair, kept as its regression test: the same switch and copy, with and
# without the label, both reporting.
#
# 2. The capacity correlation is still missing, in the allocation form, and the
# sibling capacity facts shipped since do not reach it. Nothing in
# analysis.copy.dest_capacity_unchecked (caller-handed parameter, cursor pair),
# self_sized_declared_array, unbounded_call_sized_stack_array or the converted
# buffer fact is emitted anywhere in resip/stack (vyql match: zero), and no
# VYQL-MEM-071/076/077/078 row appears in the scan, because this function states
# its capacity in none of the ways those facts read: no caller hands a byte count
# over, no declared array fixes the destination's size, no walk decrements a
# same-object counter as the destination advances, and no conversion temporary
# hides the buffer. The one place the capacity is stated is the allocation's own
# size expression, and no fact reads an allocation size at all — `new char[newSize]`
# carries no label, and resipMin carries none either.
#
# What the scanner reports on the defect is therefore unchanged and still
# inverted: VYQL-MEM-016 fires on the growth memcpy at both revisions — :534 at
# the parent, :564 at the fix, byte-for-byte the same statement — and the fix
# adds one more at :493 on the safe overhang copy it introduces. Whole
# resip/stack subtree (435 C/C++ files), three --cache off runs per side, each
# side's three runs identical: 1496 findings / 1706 rule-location rows at the
# parent against 1497 / 1707 at the fix, and every row that differs is either a
# line shift inside ConnectionBase.cxx or that added :493. The patched revision
# scores higher.
#
# Why a fourth fact is not justified today, measured rather than assumed. The
# unrestricted structural form — an allocation whose size is a local a call
# assigned, followed by a copy of a different length — was enumerated over 33
# C/C++ trees of the corpus clones: 9 sites, of which 8 are safe (a calloc whose
# element count the copy multiplies out, a strlen-sized buffer copied one byte
# shorter, a sizeof-sum allocation copied for one of its two terms, and copies
# into a different buffer entirely). Tightening to "the copy length's own
# identifier appears inside the size call's arguments" leaves 3 sites: this one,
# a sizeof-sum, and a strnlen — and the discriminator between them is the
# callee's arithmetic (min reaches below its operand; a sum and a bounded strlen
# do not). Expressing that needs either a name list of min-like helpers, whose
# only entry that catches this code is the project's own private template
# resipMin — a binding nobody would write from documentation they do not have —
# or the general correlation the engine lacks: whether an allocation's size
# expression can evaluate below the length of the copy into it. The general
# textual form is measured worthless as a signal: 184 sites across the same 33
# trees where a copy's length differs from the allocation it lands in, and the
# ordinary safe idiom (allocate len + 1, copy len) is nearly all of them. Not
# mechanical: a new frontend fact for allocation sizes plus a new
# arithmetic relation between two expressions, not a localized correction to a
# known extraction path.
#
# The first two snippets hold the real PartialBody shape at both revisions with
# the label and the switch kept; they assert VYQL-MEM-016 at both, which pins
# the inverted discrimination, and reject VYQL-MEM-071, the shipped
# destination-capacity judgment this form would join. When an allocation-side
# capacity fact lands — joined to that binding or minted beside it — the
# vulnerable snippet must flip to expect it and the asserted form must stay
# rejected: the two differ only in the >= guard and the assert relating
# contentLength to mBufferSize.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention, engine gap

test "rank1670: the body-complete guard is an exact equality, so an over-long read falls into the growth branch sized from the declared Content-Length"
  lang cpp
  file ConnectionBase.cxx
  expect VYQL-MEM-016
  reject VYQL-MEM-071
  code
  ```
  #include <stddef.h>
  #include <string.h>

  template<class T> T resipMin(T a, T b) { return a < b ? a : b; }

  #define UInt32 unsigned int
  struct HeaderValue { unsigned int value() const; };
  struct SipMessage {
     HeaderValue const_header(int) const;
     void addBuffer(char*);
     void setBody(char*, unsigned int);
  };
  enum ConnState { NewMessage, ReadingHeaders, PartialBody };

  struct ConnectionBase {
     ConnState mConnState;
     char *mBuffer;
     size_t mBufferPos;
     size_t mBufferSize;
     SipMessage *mMessage;

     static const int h_ContentLength = 20;

     // ConnectionBase::preparseNewBytes, case PartialBody, at the fix's parent
     // (resip/stack/ConnectionBase.cxx:454-537). The `start:` label is real:
     // the NewMessage state jumps back to it when a read carried a following
     // message's first bytes.
     bool preparseNewBytes(int bytesRead)
     {
     start:
        switch (mConnState)
        {
        case PartialBody:
        {
           size_t contentLength = 0;
           contentLength = mMessage->const_header(h_ContentLength).value();

           mBufferPos += bytesRead;
           if (mBufferPos == contentLength)
           {
              mMessage->addBuffer(mBuffer);
              mMessage->setBody(mBuffer, (UInt32)contentLength);
              mBuffer = 0;
              mConnState = NewMessage;
           }
           else if (mBufferPos == mBufferSize)
           {
              size_t newSize = resipMin(mBufferSize*3/2, contentLength);
              char* newBuffer = new char[newSize];
              memcpy(newBuffer, mBuffer, mBufferSize);
              mBufferSize = newSize;
              delete [] mBuffer;
              mBuffer = newBuffer;
           }
           break;
        }
        default:
           break;
        }
        return true;
     }
  };
  ```

test "rank1670: the fixed revision accepts an over-long read, carries the tail into a fresh buffer, and asserts the growth branch's precondition"
  lang cpp
  file ConnectionBase_fixed.cxx
  expect VYQL-MEM-016
  reject VYQL-MEM-071
  code
  ```
  #include <stddef.h>
  #include <string.h>
  #include <assert.h>

  template<class T> T resipMin(T a, T b) { return a < b ? a : b; }

  #define UInt32 unsigned int
  struct HeaderValue { unsigned int value() const; };
  struct SipMessage {
     HeaderValue const_header(int) const;
     void addBuffer(char*);
     void setBody(char*, unsigned int);
  };
  enum ConnState { NewMessage, ReadingHeaders, PartialBody };

  struct ConnectionBase {
     ConnState mConnState;
     char *mBuffer;
     size_t mBufferPos;
     size_t mBufferSize;
     SipMessage *mMessage;

     static const int h_ContentLength = 20;
     static const int ChunkSize = 2048;
     char* allocateBuffer(int size);

     // Patched form (resip/stack/ConnectionBase.cxx:474-566 at the fix). The
     // growth-branch memcpy is byte-for-byte the pre-fix code; only its
     // reachability changed, and the assert is what now relates contentLength
     // to mBufferSize.
     bool preparseNewBytes(int bytesRead)
     {
     start:
        switch (mConnState)
        {
        case PartialBody:
        {
           size_t contentLength = 0;
           contentLength = mMessage->const_header(h_ContentLength).value();

           mBufferPos += bytesRead;
           if (mBufferPos >= contentLength)
           {
              int overHang = mBufferPos - (int)contentLength;
              char *overHangStart = mBuffer + contentLength;

              mMessage->addBuffer(mBuffer);
              mMessage->setBody(mBuffer, (UInt32)contentLength);
              mConnState = NewMessage;
              mBuffer = 0;

              if (overHang > 0)
              {
                 size_t size = overHang * 3 / 2;
                 if (size < (size_t)ChunkSize)
                 {
                    size = ChunkSize;
                 }
                 char* newBuffer = allocateBuffer((int)size);
                 memcpy(newBuffer, overHangStart, overHang);
                 mBuffer = newBuffer;
                 mBufferPos = 0;
                 mBufferSize = size;

                 bytesRead = overHang;
              }
           }
           else if (mBufferPos == mBufferSize)
           {
              assert(contentLength >= mBufferSize);
              size_t newSize = resipMin(mBufferSize*3/2, contentLength);
              char* newBuffer = new char[newSize];
              memcpy(newBuffer, mBuffer, mBufferSize);
              mBufferSize = newSize;
              delete [] mBuffer;
              mBuffer = newBuffer;
           }
           break;
        }
        default:
           break;
        }
        return true;
     }
  };
  ```

test "rank1670: a copy inside a labelled switch is in the graph"
  lang cpp
  file labelled_switch.cxx
  expect VYQL-MEM-016
  code
  ```
  #include <stddef.h>
  #include <string.h>

  struct Conn {
     int st;
     char *mBuffer;
     size_t mBufferPos;
     size_t mBufferSize;

     bool grow(int bytesRead)
     {
     start:
        switch (st)
        {
        case 0:
           mBufferPos += bytesRead;
           break;
        case 1:
        {
           size_t newSize = mBufferSize*3/2;
           char *newBuffer = new char[newSize];
           memcpy(newBuffer, mBuffer, mBufferSize);
           mBufferSize = newSize;
           break;
        }
        }
        return true;
     }
  };
  ```

test "rank1670: the same switch and copy with no label reports identically"
